    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** leading the charge, posting an elite 83.29 score against Ryan Johnson. This matchup is our highest-value play, driven by a generous 5.15 xERA and a substantial +14% boost from our dynamic platoon modeling, effectively leveraging **Gunnar Henderson** at the top of the order. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Andy Pages** (74.02) are primed for high-output days. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong platoon advantage against JR Ritchie, while **Andy Pages** enjoys a favorable spot against a Rojas-led pitching staff. While we are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for many, these three remain locked as the core pillars of our offensive strategy to capitalize on weak opposing arms.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal slot occupied by **Dominic Smith** (43.88). He only barely edged out **Josh Jung** (54.92), who was arguably a more talented hitter but faced a tougher matchup against Alcantara, which ultimately suppressed his efficiency score below our threshold for starting. We remain cautious with **Dominic Smith** given his bottom-of-the-order projection, but his inclusion is necessitated by the need to manage our game caps while keeping our more high-ceiling assets fresh. We also considered **Miguel Vargas** for his leadoff potential, but his negative SP skill adjustment against Messick made him a sub-optimal start compared to our current utility and OF depth.\n\nRisk management is paramount today as we navigate several \"Lineup Pending\" designations. Specifically, the potential for **Jacob Wilson** (69.39) to face Robbie Ray in windy conditions provides a unique ceiling, but the volatility of his official order placement could shift his dynamic platoon edge. Additionally, we are actively fading **Nasim Nunez** and **Curtis Mead** on the bench; while **Nasim Nunez** offers potential stolen base value, the combination of a tough matchup against Luzardo and a bottom-tier batting order position makes him a liability for our 5x5 Roto averages. We are proceeding with this lineup to maximize efficiency across all categories while keeping a close eye on late-afternoon lineup confirmations.",
